WEBVTT

00:22:28.165 --> 00:22:31.102
Some people think this practice
is smart and efficient,

00:22:31.126 --> 00:22:33.714
others find it dehumanizing and spooky.

00:22:34.221 --> 00:22:37.094
Personally, I think
it's scientifically irresponsible,

00:22:37.118 --> 00:22:39.491
if not unjust and unethical.

00:22:40.449 --> 00:22:41.600
After years of research,

00:22:41.624 --> 00:22:44.297
Cade is an advocate
for something more reasonable,

00:22:44.321 --> 00:22:46.519
building algorithms
that automate the process

00:22:46.543 --> 00:22:50.446
of selecting candidates
based on key skills and values.

00:22:50.470 --> 00:22:51.851
Instead of relying on humans

00:22:51.875 --> 00:22:54.677
to integrate all the information
gathered on candidates,

00:22:54.701 --> 00:22:56.446
the algorithm weighs the information

00:22:56.470 --> 00:22:57.994
and makes the decision.

00:22:58.018 --> 00:23:00.750
CM: The number one thing
that an algorithm does,